\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{For a category \code{J} (discrete, i.e. \code{J : Category}) and a Segal category \code{C}, a \code{J}-diagram in \code{C} is a point of \code{Map(N J, C)} (→ \ref{dec-rt-0008} applied to the Segal categories \code{N J} and \code{C} viewed inside \code{Mat(Kan)}; before \ref{ms-0006}, inside \code{Vert} of the ambient VDC∞). Diagrams of shape a Segal category \code{K} are points of \code{Map(K, C)}.}
}
